+## Why
+
+Our services need one standard way to refer to a value inside a JSON document. RFC 6901 (JSON Pointer) is that standard, and later features of the toolkit will build on it.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, which returns the value a JSON Pointer refers to.
+- It throws if the pointer is not syntactically valid per RFC 6901, or if it does not resolve to a value of the document.
+- The URI fragment representation (`#/a/b`) is out of scope; only the string representation is supported.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-pointer`: parsing and evaluation of RFC 6901 JSON Pointers against a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New code in `src/` (first source file of the package); no dependencies added.
+- Public API of the library gains `resolvePointer`.
